"type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":652,"digest":"sha256:8d6d95d9661ee98a0982b7ceb9d8cc71bd219df0603e5f7f7e30f2a224153088","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-16T17:28:53Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T17:28:53Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m123-v0.12.3/m12stage3-starter-manifest.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/tarball/m123-v0.12.3","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/zipball/m123-v0.12.3","body":"# Engacer OS M12.3 / 0.12.3 — desktop and shortcuts\n\nNative qualification passes **M12-STAGE3-VM-v1** on 16 November 2026.\n[Exact-source acceptance](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/06c9aa186e8443d0e207576256b838fd9b1cf1e4/evidence/M12/3/acceptance-results.json) verifies\n574 compiled inputs, fourteen build/ZIP digests, seventeen native icon\ncomparisons and twelve cached/full movement comparisons. Public media and\nfresh complete website verification close separately before M12.4.\n\nBuild: `d7e649efbacc08139ee701199d951eeb`.\nISO SHA256: `7fa3a8507e6234ac1f29c12e94ae46811b35c702d1fa282b11dea86300d49cb3`.\nVMware ZIP SHA256: `2fb37941bb0297c66ab9cc55f4dac9fd3617ab8be8d7a56a65a67918dce1263f`.\n\n## What changes\n\nThe desktop uses one aligned grid with original 48-pixel icons, centered native\nInter labels, two-line ellipsis, full-name readback and distinct hover,\nselection and focus. Previous/Next expose overflow; disabled page buttons have\nno activation target. New objects are selected and revealed. Spatial keys skip\nempty or hidden reference cells. A single click selects; double-click or Enter\nopens. Tab activation uses the same validated route.\n\nMy files, Documents, Appearance and Recycle Bin are independent references.\nRight-click one to **Hide desktop icon**; the background menu's **Restore\ndesktop icons** brings them back. Even a genuinely empty desktop with all four\nhidden can reach Settings through Start and restore them after restart. These\ndisplay choices do not remove apps, required services or user files.\n\nReal creation, rename, shortcuts, folder pins, recycle and original-location\nRestore retain checked native storage operations. A document-and-arrow icon\nidentifies a reference without reading or executing its target during painting.\nDeleting the shortcut preserves its target. Recycling a pinned folder removes\nits pin; Restore restores the object and the user can pin it again.\n\nCaption/grip capture suppresses hover on objects behind a moving window.\nThe test caught the earlier wrong hover/full-name state; the corrected build's\ncomplete viewport matches full repaint at all twelve tested positions/scales.\nThis is rendering correctness, not an FPS or GPU-acceleration claim.\n\nFixed desktop BSS/data is **544,196 bytes**, **32 bytes** above M12.2. The hidden\nreference preference occupies **16 bytes on disk**. Desktop tasks and reference\nchanges retain zero additional managed pages and no new allocation failures;\nidle CPUs halt. There is no new icon cache, idle animation or per-window image.\n[Measured resources](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/06c9aa186e8443d0e207576256b838fd9b1cf1e4/evidence/M12/3/resources.json) and\n[how/why decisions](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/06c9aa186e8443d0e207576256b838fd9b1cf1e4/docs/architecture/desktop-m123.md) separate these quantities\nfrom configured VM RAM and total kernel consumption.\n\n## Install and try\n\n[Follow the eight-step VMware guide](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/06c9aa186e8443d0e207576256b838fd9b1cf1e4/docs/handbook/install-m123.md), then\n[use the desktop and shortcuts](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/06c9aa186e8443d0e207576256b838fd9b1cf1e4/docs/handbook/desktop-m123.md).\nUse `EngacerOS-M12STAGE3-VMware.zip` or its matching\n`EngacerOS-M12STAGE3.iso`. The ZIP contains a new blank growable 20-GiB SATA disk,\n128 MiB configured RAM, two CPUs and UEFI with Secure Boot off. Every shipped\ndevice stays enabled. The matching ISO may remain connected after installation.\n\nTwenty release assets include media, native images/maps, both manifests,\nnotices, corresponding 7-Zip source and license material.\n`M12STAGE3-SHA256SUMS.txt` covers the other nineteen files.\n[Official release](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/tag/m123-v0.12.3).\n\n## Qualification and retained limits\n\nThe exact enabled-device VMware ZIP and separate QEMU SATA/UEFI and BIOS journeys\ninstall, restart with their ISO retained and boot twice from disk. Native tasks\ncover marquee/context/keyboard selection, rename, pins, references, recycle and\nRestore, thirty-three GUI-created overflow folders, disabled paging and actual\n150%/3840×2160 display. Independent stored directories, pin bytes, the new\n16-byte preference and bundled guide are checked. A separate fresh empty-desktop\ninstallation and disk-only restart verify recovery with every reference hidden.\nAgent visual/task review is distinct from a human usability study.\n\nFree icon placement, arbitrary Unicode filenames, universal hardware/Windows\ncompatibility, ARM and vendor GPU 3D are not qualified. Existing entry/name,\nwindow and provider limits remain. Files, taskbar and later desktop refinements\ncontinue in the approved M12 order; complete final regression remains M12.18.\n\n**Retained open observation:** an earlier M12.2 candidate had a concurrent BIOS\nAHCI installation timeout. Its repeat passed, but the trigger is not isolated;\nstress reliability remains unqualified. M12.3's passing named journeys do not\nresolve that observation. Final M12.18 qualification must revisit it.\n"}